[Opening "Italian Game: Classical Variation, Giuoco Pianissimo, with d6"]

{Italian Game: Classical Variation, Giuoco Pianissimo, with d6. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. d3 Nf6 5. c3 d6 {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. h3 a5 7. O-O h6 8. Bb5 ! Bd7 {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... a4 Nbd2 a3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Nbd2 O-O 10. Re1 Re8 11. Nf1 Ne7 ?! 12. Bxd7 Qxd7 13. d4 Bb6 14. Be3 Qb5 15. Ng3 Qxb2 16. Qd3 Ng6 17. a4 Qb3 18. Nd2 Qe6 19. d5 Qd7 20. Bxb6 cxb6 21. Nc4 Qc7 22. Na3 Nf4 23. Qe3 Qd7 24. Nb5 g6 25. Ne2 N6h5 26. Qxb6 Red8 27. Qe3 Rac8 28. Ng3 Nf6 29. Nf1 h5 30. Rec1 h4 31. c4 Qe7 32. c5 Rxc5 33. Rxc5 dxc5 34. Nd2 N6xd5 35. exd5 Qg5 36. Qf3 f5 37. Nc3 e4 38. Ndxe4 fxe4 39. Nxe4 Qe5 40. Re1 Nxd5 41. Rd1 Re8 42. Nxc5 Nc3 43. Nd7 Qe2 44. Nf6+ Kf8 45. Nh7+ Kg8 46. Nf6+ {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} Kf8 1/2-1/2

[Event "Bishop versus knight: Chapter 2"]
[ChapterName "The critical sideline"]
[Date "2026.08.20"]
[Round "2"]
[White "Ding Liren"]
[Black "Duda, J-K"]
[Result "1/2-1/2"]
[WhiteElo "2847"]
[BlackElo "2912"]
[ECO "E50"]
[Opening "Nimzo-Indian Defense"]

{Nimzo-Indian Defense. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 O-O 5. Nf3 Bxc3+ {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. bxc3 d6 7. Bd3 e5 8. e4 ! Re8 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... exd4 Rb1 dxc3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. O-O exd4 10. cxd4 Nxe4 11. Re1 Nf6 ?! 12. Rxe8+ Qxe8 13. h3 Nbd7 14. Qc2 Qd8 15. Bd2 Nf8 16. Re1 Bd7 17. Bg5 h6 18. Bh4 Be8 19. g4 Ng6 20. Bg3 Nf8 21. Bh4 Ng6 22. Bg3 a6 23. Nh4 Nxh4 24. Bxh4 Rb8 25. Qe2 Bd7 26. g5 hxg5 27. Bxg5 c5 28. d5 b5 29. Bc2 bxc4 30. Kh2 Kf8 31. a3 Rb2 32. Qxc4 Kg8 33. Re3 Bf5 34. Ba4 Bd7 35. Bc2 Bf5 36. Ba4 Bd7 37. Rf3 Bxa4 38. Bxf6 gxf6 39. Qxa4 Qe7 40. Qg4+ Kf8 41. Kg2 Qe5 42. Qc8+ Ke7 43. Qc7+ Ke8 44. Qc8+ Ke7 45. Qc7+ Ke8 46. a4 Qg5+ 47. Kf1 Qc1+ 48. Kg2 Qg5+ 49. Kf1 Qc1+ 50. Kg2 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} Qg5+ 1/2-1/2

